        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333893/comment/12381618",
          "id": "12381618",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "Somehow I can't help thinking that SOCKS parameters do not really belong to\nHostConfiguration. I would rather see them in HttpState or in the HttpParam\ncollection. I suggest we address this problem in the 3.0 (4.0, that is) timeframe.\n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2004-04-24T21:39:11.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-04-24T21:39:11.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333893/comment/12381619",
          "id": "12381619",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "I agree that this probably won't make it in until the release after next (4.0).  In the mean time we could \nrefactor it into a stand-alone Socket factory and include it in contrib.  How does that sound?\n\nMike",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=becke%40u.washington.edu",
            "name": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "key": "becke@u.washington.edu",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Michael Becke",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "created": "2004-04-26T05:06:56.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-04-26T05:06:56.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333893/comment/12381620",
          "id": "12381620",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sberlin%40limepeer.com",
            "name": "sberlin@limepeer.com",
            "key": "sberlin@limepeer.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Sam Berlin",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Whatever's easiest for you folks is fine for us.  We're going to continue using \na customized version of HttpClient for the indefinite future, so it doesn't \nmuch matter where it goes in the official version.\n\nStoring the SOCKS info in HostConfiguration was more because we consider a \nSOCKS proxy to be on the same footing as an HTTP Proxy (in the sense that \nthey're both proxies), and HTTP proxy was stored in HostConfig.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=sberlin%40limepeer.com",
            "name": "sberlin@limepeer.com",
            "key": "sberlin@limepeer.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
