        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333893/comment/12381621",
          "id": "12381621",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "body": "That's the point. I can't help thinking that proxy settings do not really belong\nto HostConfiguration at all, as one would very rarely need to change proxy on a\nper host basis. In the overwhelming majority of cases there's only one proxy the\nuser would want to deal with. So, I'd rather see proxy settings moved to\nHttpParams, but that would be too radical for 3.0. \n\nOleg",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=olegk",
            "name": "olegk",
            "key": "olegk",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Oleg Kalnichevski",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Europe/Berlin"
          },
          "created": "2004-04-26T05:43:45.000+0000",
          "updated": "2004-04-26T05:43:45.000+0000"
        },
        {
          "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/issue/12333893/comment/12381622",
          "id": "12381622",
          "author": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dennis%40bevocal.com",
            "name": "dennis@bevocal.com",
            "key": "dennis@bevocal.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
              "48x48": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?avatarId=10452",
              "24x24": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=small&avatarId=10452",
              "16x16": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=xsmall&avatarId=10452",
              "32x32": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/useravatar?size=medium&avatarId=10452"
            },
            "displayName": "Dennis Cook",
            "active": true,
            "timeZone": "Etc/UTC"
          },
          "body": "Just one comment, please keep in mind those of us that use multi-homed hosts.  \nThere can be times where traffic on one NIC will require use a a proxy where \ntraffic directed through another will not.",
          "updateAuthor": {
            "self": "https://issues.apache.org/jira/rest/api/2/user?username=dennis%40bevocal.com",
            "name": "dennis@bevocal.com",
            "key": "dennis@bevocal.com",
            "avatarUrls": {
